# UI Style and Theming

## Design tokens

All colors, fonts, spacing, radius, shadow, and transition values are defined as CSS custom properties in `src/styles/tokens.css`. Never hard-code values in component CSS.

## Brand

- Primary: `var(--color-primary)` (`#0ea5e9` — sky blue)
- Primary dark: `var(--color-primary-dark)` (`#0284c7`)
- Accent: `var(--color-accent)` (`#f97316` — orange)
- Background: `var(--color-bg)` (`#f1f5f9`)
- Surface: `var(--color-surface)` (`#ffffff`)
- Text: `var(--color-text)` (`#1e293b`)
- Muted: `var(--color-muted)` (`#64748b`)
- Success: `var(--color-success)` (`#16a34a`)
- Danger: `var(--color-danger)` (`#dc2626`)

## CSS conventions

- Each component has its own `.css` file imported directly in the `.tsx`.
- Class names use BEM-lite: `.component__element--modifier`.
- No global classes except those in `base.css` and `tokens.css`.
- Never use `!important` except in `base.css` for resets.
- Responsive: mobile-first. Base styles target mobile; use `min-width` media queries for wider screens.
- No fixed pixel widths on layout containers — use `%`, `vw`, `max-width`.

## Mobile UX

- Minimum tap target: 44×44 px (enforce via `min-height` / `min-width` on buttons and list items).
- Bottom-safe-area padding: use `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)` for content near the bottom edge.
- Font size: minimum `16px` for inputs to prevent iOS auto-zoom.
- Use `var(--space-N)` tokens (4 px base grid: `--space-1` = 4px, `--space-2` = 8px … `--space-6` = 24px, `--space-8` = 32px).

## Status colors for packing items

- `pending`: normal text
- `packed`: `var(--color-success)` with strikethrough, opacity 0.6
- `discarded`: `var(--color-danger)` with strikethrough, opacity 0.6
